# The CCNOT tape as admitted into Selvage's prelude (patch 0003, ruling G7): the record
# CcnotTape and the rules tape_tick, draw and birth, with no request group.  conform.selv runs it
# against moop's trace, tests/tape_vectors.txt.
# Two circular tapes of bits, a and b, under heads i and j.  One tick fires two CCNOTs that share
# their controls, the cells under both heads, and target the next cell of each tape; then head i
# moves forward and head j backward.  It is wiring 1 of moop's tape, and a trace of moop's own
# implementation pins it bit for bit (VI.6).  Each tape needs at least two cells, or a target
# would be a control: R4 refuses that when it runs.
type CcnotTape(a: Array(Bit), b: Array(Bit), i: I64, j: I64)

rule tape_tick takes CcnotTape returns CcnotTape
    CcnotTape(a, b, i, j) <-> CcnotTape(a, b, ni, nj) where
        add a[i] * b[j] to a[(i + 1) mod length(a)]
        add a[i] * b[j] to b[(j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)]
        ni is (i + 1) mod length(a)
        i was (ni + length(a) - 1) mod length(a)
        nj is (j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)
        j was (nj + 1) mod length(b)

# A draw ticks the tape and copies the cell then under head i: a deterministic observation of the
# tape, not a random bit.  It is a rule, not a request, so nothing else can be the tape's draw.
rule draw takes CcnotTape returns (Bit, CcnotTape)
    s <-> (seen, s) where
        s is tape_tick(s)
        seen is s.a[s.i]

# A birth draws one cell for each cell of a child tape, a's first, and gives the child with the
# parent.  The tape a program draws from is the one it makes and passes along; the tapes it
# starts from are where it starts, not a source of entropy.
rule birth takes CcnotTape returns (CcnotTape, CcnotTape)
    s <-> (CcnotTape(ca, cb, 0, 0), s) where
        ca is array(Bit, length(s.a))
        cb is array(Bit, length(s.b))
        repeat with k from 0 to length(ca) - 1
            s is tape_tick(s)
            add s.a[s.i] to ca[k]
        repeat with k from 0 to length(cb) - 1
            s is tape_tick(s)
            add s.a[s.i] to cb[k]
